de1-node3 (CentOS Stream 10, mariadb-server 10.11.18 + mariadb-server-galera), loaded application data (appdb.orders), then added node4 as a fourth member via SST (mariabackup), verified it carries the existing data and accepts writes that replicate to all peers. Along the way fixed two environment issues: wrong wsrep_provider path (galera-4 -> galera) and an SELinux AVC denial blocking mariadb-backup's connectto to its own mysqld_t socket, resolved with a minimal custom SELinux module (mariabackup_sst) installed on all 4 nodes. Firewall ports 3306/4567(tcp+udp)/4568/4444 opened via firewalld on all nodes; mariadb enabled at boot on all 4. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on node1, node2, node3, then node4: captured boot_id baseline, issued systemctl reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed boot_id changed, and confirmed each node auto-rejoined with wsrep_cluster_size=4, state Synced, status Primary, and appdb.orders intact (4 rows) before moving to the next node. Final cross-node check shows all 4 nodes consistent.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected all 4 nodes: CentOS Stream 10, no MariaDB pre-installed\",\"Installed mariadb-server + mariadb-server-galera on node1-4\",\"Added CLUSTER_HOSTS to /etc/hosts on all nodes\",\"Opened firewalld ports 3306/tcp,4567/tcp,4567/udp,4568/tcp,4444/tcp on all nodes; confirmed SELinux mysqld_port_t already covers these ports\",\"Set up cluster SSH keypair on all nodes for secure file distribution\",\"Generated SST and root passwords on node1, distributed via scp (never printed)\",\"Wrote Galera config (wsrep_cluster_address=gcomm://node1,node2,node3) on node1-3; fixed wsrep_provider path from /usr/lib64/galera-4 to /usr/lib64/galera\",\"Diagnosed SELinux AVC denial (mysqld_t connectto self unix_stream_socket) blocking mariadb-backup SST; built and installed custom policy module mariabackup_sst.pp on all 4 nodes\",\"Bootstrapped node1 with galera_new_cluster, created sstuser and set root password, created appdb.orders with 3 seed rows\",\"Started mariadb on node2 (cleared stale datadir from earlier failed SST, retried successfully) and node3; verified cluster_size 2 then 3, Synced/Primary, data replicated\",\"Enabled mariadb at boot on node1-3\",\"Updated wsrep_cluster_address to include node4 on node1-3; wrote node4 galera.cnf; started mariadb on node4\",\"Verified node4 joined with cluster_size 4, existing data present, then inserted a row from node4 and confirmed it replicated to node1-3\",\"Enabled mariadb at boot on node4\",\"Captured boot_id baseline and health for all 4 nodes\",\"Sequentially rebooted node1, node2, node3, node4 one at a time (systemctl reboot backgrounded for ack-before-disconnect), polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, verified cluster_size 4/Synced/Primary and appdb.orders row count after each before proceeding to next node\",\"Performed final consistency check across nodes\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"3-node Galera cluster established on node1-3 with application data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-59d804749233476f\",\"cmd-52fcf17183c04f51\",\"cmd-7c4b7950782d4590\",\"cmd-48dc941995de46f9\"],\"summary\":\"node1 bootstrapped (cluster_size=1, Synced, Primary), appdb.orders seeded with 3 rows; node2 joined via SST (cluster_size=2, data present); node3 joined (cluster_size=3, Synced, Primary, data present)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node4 added as 4th member carrying existing data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-59142800b4df4afb\",\"cmd-88ffb84d1f144aae\"],\"summary\":\"node4 mariadb started, joined cluster via SST; wsrep_cluster_size=4, Synced, Primary, and appdb.orders shows all 3 original rows\"},{\"requirement\":\"node4 accepts writes like other members\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b93f29d9529e48e6\",\"cmd-4e48be3fe77445c1\",\"cmd-40f1b14e0a924695\",\"cmd-3dd5b5cc6c514c65\"],\"summary\":\"Inserted a row on node4; row visible identically on node1, node2, and node3, confirming multi-master write acceptance and replication\"},{\"requirement\":\"Environment troubleshooting (galera provider path, SELinux SST denial)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-507b90aa28ca47ea\",\"cmd-1842be7471214a37\",\"cmd-991acf3b1d544489\",\"cmd-97fd118afc904df3\",\"cmd-6cc585cc4a404caa\"],\"summary\":\"Diagnosed wrong provider .so path and an SELinux AVC connectto denial blocking mariadb-backup SST; fixed provider path and installed a custom SELinux policy module allowing the specific denial\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2ce9d63f011d4e3d\",\"cmd-8ac67c34f0f348ff\",\"cmd-d584790472984a17\",\"cmd-8a1eee0ccd134f1d\",\"cmd-41f76ae4ea664412\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 0581c914...; reboot acknowledged; node unreachable during reboot; new boot_id 76e46f6e... confirms restart; post-restart cluster_size=4, Synced, Primary, 4 rows present\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6db0434c419b45d7\",\"cmd-603af3d00ca54946\",\"cmd-3c08b5e39174494f\",\"cmd-56b673ea8738428c\",\"cmd-83dedfd33f9d415f\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id be303eb3...; reboot acknowledged; node unreachable during reboot; new boot_id 5116edd2... confirms restart; post-restart cluster_size=4, Synced, Primary, 4 rows present\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-893b52ffbe314f8c\",\"cmd-71d7820681e54a1f\",\"cmd-0e4b048da823466e\",\"cmd-53b5018292f14d27\",\"cmd-3ad6ac728f054ff8\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 21de1f79...; reboot acknowledged; node unreachable during reboot; new boot_id 94157f51... confirms restart; post-restart cluster_size=4, Synced, Primary, 4 rows present\"},{\"requirement\":\"node4 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ec3443a6a0f84c15\",\"cmd-0b8d2e8fc39d4fb2\",\"cmd-925c180d053b4451\",\"cmd-70bab9b2634d43ca\",\"cmd-c74f3b590fe74be1\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 8f258838...; reboot acknowledged; node unreachable during reboot; new boot_id d544cf97... confirms restart; post-restart cluster_size=4, Synced, Primary, 4 rows present\"},{\"requirement\":\"Final cross-cluster consistency after all restarts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-63bcac3b6603402e\"],\"summary\":\"node1 shows cluster_size=4 and all 4 orders rows consistent after full restart cycle across all nodes\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Built a 3-node MariaDB Galera cluster on node1-node3 (CentOS Stream 10, mariadb-server 10.11.18 + mariadb-server-galera), loaded application data (appdb.orders), then added node4 as a fourth member via SST (mariabackup), verified it carries the existing data and accepts writes that replicate to all peers. Along the way fixed two environment issues: wrong wsrep_provider path (galera-4 -> galera) and an SELinux AVC denial blocking mariadb-backup's connectto to its own mysqld_t socket, resolved with a minimal custom SELinux module (mariabackup_sst) installed on all 4 nodes. Firewall ports 3306/4567(tcp+udp)/4568/4444 opened via firewalld on all nodes; mariadb enabled at boot on all 4. Completed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart protocol on node1, node2, node3, then node4: captured boot_id baseline, issued systemctl reboot, polled until reachable, confirmed boot_id changed, and confirmed each node auto-rejoined with wsrep_cluster_size=4, state Synced, status Primary, and appdb.orders intact (4 rows) before moving to the next node. Final cross-node check shows all 4 nodes consistent.","actions_performed":["Inspected all 4 nodes: CentOS Stream 10, no MariaDB pre-installed","Installed mariadb-server + mariadb-server-galera on node1-4","Added CLUSTER_HOSTS to /etc/hosts on all nodes","Opened firewalld ports 3306/tcp,4567/tcp,4567/udp,4568/tcp,4444/tcp on all nodes; confirmed SELinux mysqld_port_t already covers these ports","Set up cluster SSH keypair on all nodes for secure file distribution","Generated SST and root passwords on node1, distributed via scp (never printed)","Wrote Galera config (wsrep_cluster_address=gcomm://node1,node2,node3) on node1-3; fixed wsrep_provider path from /usr/lib64/galera-4 to /usr/lib64/galera","Diagnosed SELinux AVC denial (mysqld_t connectto self unix_stream_socket) blocking mariadb-backup SST; built and installed custom policy module mariabackup_sst.pp on all 4 nodes","Bootstrapped node1 with galera_new_cluster, created sstuser and set root password, created appdb.orders with 3 seed rows","Started mariadb on node2 (cleared stale datadir from earlier failed SST, retried successfully) and node3; verified cluster_size 2 then 3, Synced/Primary, data replicated","Enabled mariadb at boot on node1-3","Updated wsrep_cluster_address to include node4 on node1-3; wrote node4 galera.cnf; started mariadb on node4","Verified node4 joined with cluster_size 4, existing data present, then inserted a row from node4 and confirmed it replicated to node1-3","Enabled mariadb at boot on node4","Captured boot_id baseline and health for all 4 nodes","Sequentially rebooted node1, node2, node3, node4 one at a time (systemctl reboot backgrounded for ack-before-disconnect), polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id, verified cluster_size 4/Synced/Primary and appdb.orders row count after each before proceeding to next node","Performed final consistency check across nodes"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"3-node Galera cluster established on node1-3 with application data","command_ids":["cmd-59d804749233476f","cmd-52fcf17183c04f51","cmd-7c4b7950782d4590","cmd-48dc941995de46f9"],"summary":"node1 bootstrapped (cluster_size=1, Synced, Primary), appdb.orders seeded with 3 rows; node2 joined via SST (cluster_size=2, data present); node3 joined (cluster_size=3, Synced, Primary, data present)"},{"requirement":"node4 added as 4th member carrying existing data","command_ids":["cmd-59142800b4df4afb","cmd-88ffb84d1f144aae"],"summary":"node4 mariadb started, joined cluster via SST; wsrep_cluster_size=4, Synced, Primary, and appdb.orders shows all 3 original rows"},{"requirement":"node4 accepts writes like other members","command_ids":["cmd-b93f29d9529e48e6","cmd-4e48be3fe77445c1","cmd-40f1b14e0a924695","cmd-3dd5b5cc6c514c65"],"summary":"Inserted a row on node4; row visible identically on node1, node2, and node3, confirming multi-master write acceptance and replication"},{"requirement":"Environment troubleshooting (galera provider path, SELinux SST denial)","command_ids":["cmd-507b90aa28ca47ea","cmd-1842be7471214a37","cmd-991acf3b1d544489","cmd-97fd118afc904df3","cmd-6cc585cc4a404caa"],"summary":"Diagnosed wrong provider .so path and an SELinux AVC connectto denial blocking mariadb-backup SST; fixed provider path and installed a custom SELinux policy module allowing the specific denial"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-2ce9d63f011d4e3d","cmd-8ac67c34f0f348ff","cmd-d584790472984a17","cmd-8a1eee0ccd134f1d","cmd-41f76ae4ea664412"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 0581c914...; reboot acknowledged; node unreachable during reboot; new boot_id 76e46f6e... confirms restart; post-restart cluster_size=4, Synced, Primary, 4 rows present"},{"requirement":"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-6db0434c419b45d7","cmd-603af3d00ca54946","cmd-3c08b5e39174494f","cmd-56b673ea8738428c","cmd-83dedfd33f9d415f"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id be303eb3...; reboot acknowledged; node unreachable during reboot; new boot_id 5116edd2... confirms restart; post-restart cluster_size=4, Synced, Primary, 4 rows present"},{"requirement":"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state","command_ids":["cmd-893b52ffbe314f8c","cmd-71d7820681e54a1f","cmd-0e4b048da823466e","cmd-53b5018292f14d27","cmd-3ad6ac728f054ff8"],"summary":"Baseline boo